    claim "C1" from-slice="TS.260821.19" state="met" \
        evidence="tests/phases.rs::an_approach_with_no_alternative_is_refused — `over` is required, \
            because an approach with nothing rejected is a description of the only thing anybody \
            thought of"
    claim "C2" from-slice="TS.260821.19" state="met" \
        evidence="tests/phases.rs::implementing_without_naming_the_approach_is_refused. \
            implement-follows-an-approach refuses and is witnessed. The test also asserts a \
            design-system that produced NO approach forces nothing — this refuses building against \
            no plan, never building without permission"
    claim "C3" from-slice="TS.260821.19" state="met" \
        evidence="this iteration itself. The approach was recorded before any code, and a fourth \
            approach was discovered while implementing when shaping `phase` refused a hundred and \
            sixty-six existing ones. It is on the record as a `matured` entry rather than edited \
            into the plan, so what was planned and what was learned stay distinguishable"
    claim "C4" from-slice="TS.260821.19" state="met" \
        evidence="tests/phases.rs::a_teach_phase_that_names_no_reader_is_reported. \
            teach-reaches-an-end-user reports and is witnessed; thirty-three historical teach \
            phases were back-filled with `taught=\"the-next-agent\"`, which is what they actually \
            did, so the rule landed on zero"
    claim "C5" from-slice="TS.260821.19" state="met" \
        evidence="tests/phases.rs::a_phase_is_shaped_whether_its_fields_are_nodes_or_properties. \
            `phase` has a shape and its states are a checked vocabulary rather than a prose string"

    layer "doctrine"    state="evidenced" \
        evidence="skills/plan-before-building/SKILL.md, anchored and registered. 54 of 54 anchored" \
        reaches="the phases say what each must produce, and teach says for whom"
    layer "enforcement" state="evidenced" \
        evidence="implement-follows-an-approach refuses; teach-reaches-an-end-user reports; both \
            witnessed. 26 of 54 rules witnessed, and praxis check is clean at zero reports" \
        reaches="implement complete with no approach is refused"
    layer "docs"        state="evidenced" \
        evidence="`praxis ask iteration --show phase` answers what was planned per iteration, and \
            this iteration's own approach block is the worked example" \
        reaches="`what did they consider, and why this` is answerable per iteration"

    phase "design-ux" state="complete" required-by="docs" worked-by="agent:principal-engineer" \
        produced="the refusal names the PHASE and what it should point at, not the rule"
    // `followed` is written as CHILD NODES. It was four repeated PROPERTIES, and KDL keeps
    // only the last of a repeated property — so this iteration claimed four approaches and
    // the record held one. Corrected rather than matured: nothing about the decision changed,
    // the file simply never held what was decided (ITER.260823.01/BB1).
    phase "implement" state="complete" required-by="enforcement · docs" \
        worked-by="agent:principal-engineer" \
        produced="the phase and approach kinds, the two rules with witnesses, property-aware \
            field reading, and thirty-three back-filled teach phases" {
        followed "the phase carries its own approach, and implement points at it"
        followed "four rules, and the fourth reports rather than refuses"
        followed "the schema describes a field whether it is a child node or a property"
        followed "an approach is matured, never overwritten"
    }
    phase "learn" state="complete" required-by="always" worked-by="agent:principal-engineer" \
        produced="AZ1 and AZ2 — one about what the shape exposed, one about what it still cannot see"
    phase "teach" state="skipped" required-by="doctrine" worked-by="agent:principal-engineer" \
        produced="skills/plan-before-building/SKILL.md" \
        note="taught an AGENT and says so. The reader of a release gets nothing from this slice, \
            which is now visible rather than hidden behind a skill counted twice" \
        skipped-because="it produced doctrine for an AGENT, which is the doctrine LAYER and is recorded there. Teaching an end user the feature's why and how did not happen — and the record already serves the next agent, whose own persona judges success by NOT needing a document (TS.260821.19, ITER.260822.15/BA1)"

    finding "AZ1" state="open" size="frame-sized" \
        text="`phase` was called `deliberately shapeless` and it was not a choice — the schema \
            could only describe child nodes, and phases carry their values as PROPERTIES. \
            Declaring a shape refused a hundred and sixty-six of them until the checker learned to \
            read a property as a field" \
        obliges="`condition`, `vet` and `entry` are carried as properties too and are shapeable \
            now. None is shaped; each is a separate decision" \
        note="the sixth declaration this session that read to nothing, after states=, when-state, \
            needed-by, the audit exclude list and the phase `kinds=` string. The pattern has a \
            shape: a limitation gets written down as an intention, and `deliberately shapeless` \
            is what that sounds like a year later"

    finding "BA1" state="open" size="frame-sized" \
        text="C4's evidence above is superseded and left standing, because a closed iteration is \
            history. It says thirty-three teach phases were back-filled with \
            taught=\"the-next-agent\". That was wrong twice over, and the record caught it" \
        note="TAUTOLOGY. Every iteration teaches the next agent by existing — that is what the \
            record IS, and S7 is the symptom about exactly this. A value true by construction \
            discriminates nothing, which is the argument that removed `frame` from the `serves` \
            vocabulary hours earlier. I reintroduced the defect I had just fixed" \
        note="CONTRADICTION. The next-agent persona judges success by `asking the record and \
            getting an answer it can act on, RATHER THAN A DOCUMENT IT MUST READ`. Every one of \
            those phases produced a skill file. The back-fill claimed success against a criterion \
            the artifact fails" \
        note="corrected: those thirty-four teach phases are `skipped`, with the reason. They \
            produced doctrine for an agent, which is the doctrine LAYER and is recorded there. \
            Teaching an end user did not happen, and skipped-phase-without-rationale already \
            existed for saying so. The teach phase has one reader and it is not the next agent"

    finding "AZ2" state="open" size="observation" \
        text="nothing checks that the approach was recorded BEFORE the code. A phase written at \
            close with an `over` clause satisfies every rule this slice adds" \
        note="the honest limit, and it is the same shape as AY2: order in time is not something a \
            snapshot holds, and the obvious source is git, which is outside the record" \
        note="SUPERSEDED, and the framing above is the mistake. Chronology was never the point. \
            The CODE is the decision — the plan is the educated act before it, and what it buys is \
            that the alternatives were in view when the decision was taken. A plan written at close \
            that accurately names what was rejected still delivers that; a plan written first that \
            nobody consulted delivers nothing. `was it written before` is unverifiable and also \
            not the question" \
        note="the question it should have asked is whether the approach and the code AGREE. \
            implement-follows-an-approach checks that implement NAMES one; nothing checks that the \
            named one is what got built. An approach recorded and not followed is a decision the \
            record claims was taken and was not — which is worse than no plan, and is the same \
            shape as a-value-agrees-with-its-maturation one level up. That is the finding, and it \
            is not the one AZ2 wrote"

    // Written BEFORE any code, which is the whole subject of the slice. If this iteration
    // records its approach at close like every other one in this frame, it has demonstrated
    // the defect rather than fixed it.
    phase "design-system" state="complete" worked-by="agent:principal-engineer" {
        matured "approach" {
            from "three approaches, recorded before any code existed"
            to "four — the fourth discovered while implementing, when declaring a shape for `phase` refused a hundred and sixty-six existing phases"
            at "2026-08-22"
            because "the plan did not decide whether a field is a child node or a property, and \
                the answer only appeared when the shape was applied to a record that already had \
                phases in it. Recorded as a maturation so the plan and the discovery stay \
                distinguishable — which is what this iteration is about"
            taught-by "ITER.260822.14"
        }

        approach "the phase carries its own approach, and implement points at it" {
            over "a design document per slice, under docs/ or beside the record"
            over "an approval gate between design and implement"
            over "making design-system mandatory on every slice"
            over "a free-text `plan` field with nothing checked about it"
            because "the approach belongs where the claims it will settle already are. Thirty-four \
                slices already carry a scenario and steps in exactly this shape, so the record \
                needs a place for the CHOICE rather than a new document to hold it. A separate \
                file is a second thing to keep in step, and this frame has spent the day finding \
                what happens to second copies"
            note "the approval gate was the tempting one and it is a different rule. The same \
                agent may design and build; what is refused is implementing with no approach \
                recorded. Who may ATTEST is TS.260821.08 and it already refuses"
            note "mandatory-on-every-slice was rejected because skipped-phase-without-rationale \
                already exists for the skip, and is unwitnessed. A slice whose layers do not need \
                a design phase skips it with a reason"
        }

        approach "four rules, and the fourth reports rather than refuses" {
            over "one rule doing all four checks"
            over "refusing a teach phase that names only a skill"
            because "an undeclared phase kind, an approach with no alternative, and an implement \
                with no approach are all shape violations and fail closed. Whether a teach phase \
                served an END USER is a judgement about a document, and every iteration in this \
                record would fail it today — a rule that names all fourteen on arrival is one \
                nobody adopts, which this frame has now learned twice"
            note "the order is the same one TS.260821.04 and a-claim-of-value-names-whose had to \
                use: report, take the count to zero, then flip"
        }

        approach "the schema describes a field whether it is a child node or a property" {
            over "rewriting a hundred and sixty-six existing phases into child nodes"
            over "leaving `phase` shapeless and checking its kinds some other way"
            because "declaring a shape for `phase` refused every phase in the record, because they \
                are written as PROPERTIES and the schema could only describe child nodes. That is \
                why `phase` was called `deliberately shapeless` — it was not a choice about \
                phases, it was the schema having no way to describe them. Reading a property as a \
                field removes the escape hatch entirely, and no existing record had to change"
            note "this approach was not in the plan above. It was discovered while implementing, \
                which is C3's case — matured onto the record rather than edited into the original, \
                so what was planned and what was learned stay distinguishable"
            note "the wider consequence is that `condition`, `vet` and `entry` are also carried as \
                properties and are also shapeable now. None is shaped yet, and each is a separate \
                decision"
        }

        approach "an approach is matured, never overwritten" {
            over "letting an approach be edited in place while the iteration is open"
            because "discovering the design was wrong while building is the normal case and must \
                stay cheap. TS.260821.18 shipped the shape for exactly this, and a rule that \
                punished a mid-flight correction would teach people to write the approach at close \
                — which is the behaviour being fixed"
        }
    }
    closed-at "2026-08-22T23:03:32Z"
    outcome "continue"

    close {
        claims-settled "C1" how="met"
        claims-settled "C2" how="met"
        claims-settled "C3" how="met"
        claims-settled "C4" how="met"
        claims-settled "C5" how="met"
